<title>ITALY: Mediaset has slight fall in 96 net profit.</title>
<headline>Mediaset has slight fall in 96 net profit.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31 1996</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit			445.3  vs 454.6</p>
<p>    Cons pretax profit		   835.4  vs 578.1</p>
<p>    Cons operating profit		850.3  vs 731.6</p>
<p>    Gross operating margin	    1,741.5 vs 1,561.7</p>
<p>    Cons turnover			 3,133.7 vs 2,953.8</p>
<p>    Net financial charges		   9.1 vs 226.4</p>
<p>    Cons net liquidity		   839    vs 644.6 net debt</p>
<p>    Tax charge				389.2 vs 123.8</p>
<p>    Parent company net profit	     371 vs 128.1</p>
<p>    Parent company turnover	   1,262.1 up 2.7 percent</p>
<p>Note - The company earlier announced a dividend of 195 lire against 175 lire the previous year. It said 1996 operating costs at 1,392.2 were almost unchanged from 1995. Mediastet said its Publitalia 80 advertising subsidiary reported a 10.4 percent rise in turnover in the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66102321</p>
